# Alert settings for podium: podium-alert@.service (a unit failed) and
# podium-check.timer (disk, WAL, replication, the weekly restore proof)
# read this file. install.sh alerts copies it to /etc/podium/alert.env
# (root-owned, mode 600) when it does not exist. See docs/OPERATIONS.md,
# "Alerts".

# Where alerts are posted, as an https URL that accepts a plain-text POST.
# For ntfy: https://ntfy.sh/<topic>, with a long random topic name (the
# topic is the only secret: anyone who knows it can read and send
# alerts). Pick one with: openssl rand -hex 16, then subscribe to the same
# topic in the ntfy app on your phone. A self-hosted ntfy works the same.
# Secret.
# Optional, but without it no alert reaches anyone: the alert unit then
# fails, which shows in "systemctl --failed". Default: empty.
PODIUM_ALERT_WEBHOOK=
